al division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551274 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47e4cafc-245d-597a-859f-2f903cb45c89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551274 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $5.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}={x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37988" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8611bb27-3bf5-5d1d-beee-a73906924e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551303 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+6 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a28bf299-6ff2-586b-9620-39977848687b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551318 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-2 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551355